# .dockerignore for the unified showcase frontend.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE EDITING — which file Docker actually honours depends on the
# build context:
#
#   * The compose build uses `context: ../` (the REPOSITORY ROOT). Docker only
#     applies the .dockerignore at the CONTEXT ROOT, so the file that filters
#     that build is `/.dockerignore` at the repo root. It already excludes
#     **/node_modules, **/.next, **/.git, **/dist, **/build, **/coverage,
#     **/__pycache__, **/.venv, **/*.log and the env files — everything this
#     image needs kept out. Crucially it does NOT exclude
#     showcase/integrations/*/manifest.yaml, which the Dockerfile's `manifests`
#     stage bind-mounts and MUST be able to see. (Named stage, never an ordinal
#     like "stage 2" — the Dockerfile bans ordinal references because renumbering
#     silently rots them; see its header.) Do not add an `integrations` exclusion
#     to the root file: every demo URL would then render as
#     "Invalid Showcase route".
#
#   * THIS FILE IS CURRENTLY INERT ON EVERY PATH, and that is worth knowing
#     before you edit it expecting an effect. It would only be honoured by a
#     build using THIS directory as the context (`docker build
#     showcase/frontends/nextjs`) — but no such build can run: the Dockerfile's
#     first instruction is `COPY showcase/frontends/nextjs/package.json …`,
#     a REPO-ROOT-relative path that does not exist inside an app-directory
#     context, so the build fails on that line rather than proceeding without
#     the manifests. The exclusions below are kept as documentation of what
#     such a build would need to drop, and so the file does not read as an
#     oversight — not because they filter anything today. If you need to
#     exclude something from the real image, the root `/.dockerignore` is the
#     file that does it.
#
# Same convention, and same reasoning, as showcase/shell-dashboard/.dockerignore.
#
# Files the build DOES need here (keep these visible):
#   package.json, package-lock.json, .npmrc, next.config.ts, tsconfig.json,
#   postcss.config.mjs, components.json, src/, public/

# Installed / generated trees — rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules
.next
out
dist
build
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test and tooling output.
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
.nyc_output
.turbo
.swc

# Secrets and local environment.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# VCS, editor and OS noise.
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.log

# Test tooling. SCOPE WARNING: these patterns do NOT apply to the supported build.
# That build uses `context: ../`, so only the repo-root /.dockerignore is honoured
# (see the header) and the root file has no test exclusions — its
# `COPY showcase/frontends/nextjs/ ./` therefore brings every *.test.ts / *.test.tsx
# under src/ plus vitest.config.ts into the `builder` stage. Nothing in the FINAL
# image runs them (the `runner` stage copies only .next, node_modules,
# package.json, public and next.config.ts, none of which carry test files), so the
# shipped image is clean either way; and these patterns buy NOTHING today, because
# the app-directory build they would apply to cannot run at all — see the header.
# To keep the tests out of the builder layer as well, the same patterns must be
# added to the repo-root /.dockerignore — prefixed with
# `showcase/frontends/nextjs/`, because root patterns are matched against
# context-root-relative paths.
vitest.config.ts
playwright.config.ts
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
